WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.025
"Wow," Henry said. "Who would leave a message like that?"

2
00:00:19.026 --> 00:00:21.167
"I don't know," Maggie said.

3
00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:24.373
"I thought everyone in town loved the summer parade."

4
00:00:24.374 --> 00:00:28.223
Cole shrugged. "Maybe someone is joking around."

5
00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:33.538
"If it's a joke, it's not very funny." Henry stared at the message.

6
00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:37.062
"It sounds more like a threat."

7
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:41.215
Cole grinned. "Are you trying to turn it into a mystery, Henry?"

8
00:00:41.216 --> 00:00:47.931
Just then two teenage girls, Jill and Ashley, raced up to the lemonade stand.

9
00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:51.546
"Oh my gosh! Did you guys hear what happened?" Jill asked.

10
00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:55.698
Ashley continued before The Lemonade Detectives could respond.

11
00:00:55.699 --> 00:01:00.771
"Someone broke into the shed where Mrs. Sweet is keeping her float!" she cried.

12
00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:05.080
"Huh?" Cole said. "Why would someone do that?"

13
00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:08.534
"Was the float damaged?" Henry asked.

14
00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:12.098
Jill shook her head. "We're not sure.

15
00:01:12.099 --> 00:01:18.383
Mrs. Sweet is keeping her float top secret until the parade, so she didn't tell us exactly what happened.

16
00:01:18.384 --> 00:01:21.650
But she's afraid that someone wants to sabotage it."

17
00:01:21.651 --> 00:01:26.881
Just then Ashley's cell phone rang. "Oops, we have to go," she said.

18
00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:28.611
"Come on, Jill."

19
00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:32.397
The girls raced off. Maggie looked worried.

20
00:01:32.398 --> 00:01:37.808
"This is bad. What if someone is trying to sabotage all the floats?"

21
00:01:37.809 --> 00:01:42.063
"Why would anyone do that?" Cole sounded skeptical.

22
00:01:42.064 --> 00:01:46.109
Maggie shrugged. "Maybe to win those great prizes.

23
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.820
We should probably investigate before someone tries to destroy our float!"

24
00:01:50.821 --> 00:01:56.540
"How could anybody do that?" Cole said. "It's inside your house, Maggie.

25
00:01:56.541 --> 00:02:00.751
Besides, we don't have time to mess around with a mystery right now."

26
00:02:00.752 --> 00:02:06.338
He laughed. "I don't think this is a mystery anyway. Right, Henry?"

27
00:02:06.339 --> 00:02:08.998
Henry didn't answer for a second.

28
00:02:08.999 --> 00:02:13.154
He was thinking about that threatening message on the town website.

29
00:02:13.155 --> 00:02:16.953
"Maybe we should go talk to my dad," he said.

30
00:02:16.954 --> 00:02:20.415
"Just in case something really is going on."

31
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:25.477
"Good idea," Maggie said. "Uncle Kevin is a newspaper reporter.

32
00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:29.382
It's his job to know about weird stuff happening around town."

33
00:02:29.383 --> 00:02:33.102
"Fine." Cole shrugged. "You two go talk to him.

34
00:02:33.103 --> 00:02:38.475
I'll stay here and watch the lemonade stand."

35
00:02:38.476 --> 00:02:43.711
Henry and Maggie walked toward the main part of town, where the newspaper office was located.

36
00:02:43.712 --> 00:02:46.404
On the way they passed Eddie's house.

37
00:02:46.405 --> 00:02:50.816
The garage door was shut; no music was coming from behind it.

38
00:02:50.817 --> 00:02:55.358
"I guess Snake's band isn't practicing today," Henry said.

39
00:02:55.359 --> 00:02:58.782
He told Maggie about seeing the band the day before.

40
00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:01.128
Maggie stared at the garage.

41
00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:06.189
"I wonder if Snake and his band members should be suspects," she said.

42
00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:09.757
"He seemed really excited about winning the contest."

43
00:03:09.758 --> 00:03:12.989
"Lots of people want to win," Henry said.

44
00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:17.620
"That doesn't mean all of them want to sabotage the other floats."

45
00:03:17.621 --> 00:03:22.958
"Maybe not." Maggie shrugged. "But Snake seemed kind of sneaky."

46
00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:27.043
Henry didn't answer. He thought Snake seemed okay.

47
00:03:27.044 --> 00:03:33.594
But when Maggie got an idea in her head, it could be hard to change her mind.

48
00:03:33.595 --> 00:03:37.694
A few minutes later, they reached the newspaper office.

49
00:03:37.695 --> 00:03:43.001
"Hi, Henry," the receptionist said. "Your dad just left."

50
00:03:43.002 --> 00:03:48.026
"Really?" Henry was disappointed. "Do you know when he'll be back?

51
00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:52.363
We wanted to ask him some questions about the summer parade."

52
00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:56.937
The receptionist pointed to a young man who had just come into the lobby.

53
00:03:56.938 --> 00:04:01.461
"If it's about the parade, maybe Jackson can help," she said.

54
00:04:01.462 --> 00:04:04.138
"He's assigned to cover that story."

55
00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:07.149
Henry had met Jackson several times.

56
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.803
He walked over to the reporter with Maggie right behind him.

57
00:04:11.804 --> 00:04:14.821
Jackson smiled when he saw them coming.

58
00:04:14.822 --> 00:04:18.694
"Hi, Henry," he said. "Hi, Maggie. What's up?

59
00:04:18.695 --> 00:04:23.057
Did The Lemonade Detectives uncover an exciting crime for me to write about?"

60
00:04:23.058 --> 00:04:25.265
"Maybe," Henry said.

61
00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:28.621
"Is it true that you're covering the parade this year?"

62
00:04:28.622 --> 00:04:32.279
"That's right." Jackson didn't sound very excited.

63
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.058
Henry wasn't surprised.

64
00:04:34.059 --> 00:04:39.011
His father said Jackson was always looking for important and dramatic stories.

65
00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:43.338
Unfortunately for him, there weren't very many of those in Belltown.

66
00:04:43.339 --> 00:04:48.211
"We heard someone might have tampered with Mrs. Sweet's float," Maggie spoke up.

67
00:04:48.212 --> 00:04:51.082
Jackson nodded. "I heard it too.

68
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:55.123
Actually, I was just on my way over to the Sweet Shop to talk to her.

69
00:04:55.124 --> 00:04:57.470
You two can come along, if you like."

70
00:04:57.471 --> 00:05:02.554
The three of them headed outside.

71
00:05:02.555 --> 00:05:07.086
"Do you think someone is trying to sabotage Mrs. Sweet's float?"

72
00:05:07.087 --> 00:05:10.108
Henry asked as they walked toward the Sweet Shop.

73
00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.868
Jackson shook his head. "I doubt it.

74
00:05:12.869 --> 00:05:16.578
Her float was probably damaged by animals or something.

75
00:05:16.579 --> 00:05:20.409
Or maybe she just got confused and forgot to lock the shed."

76
00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:25.799
Henry thought about that. Mrs. Sweet was always joking about her bad memory.

77
00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.877
She often said she'd forget her head if it wasn't attached to her neck!

78
00:05:29.878 --> 00:05:34.170
Could Mrs. Sweet's forgetfulness explain what Jill and Ashley had said?

79
00:05:34.171 --> 00:05:37.961
Henry was still wondering about it when they reached the Sweet Shop.

80
00:05:37.962 --> 00:05:44.826
Just then there was a blood-curdling scream from the alley beside the shop!
